        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.117,
            0.358,
            0.138
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.2,
            0.14,
            0.885,
            0.231
          ],
          "content": "1. Colour the sectors of the circle below so that the figure has i) 3 angles of symmetry, ii) 4 angles of symmetry, iii) what are the possible numbers of angles of symmetry you can obtain by colouring the sectors in different ways?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.428,
            0.238,
            0.62,
            0.383
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_21_image_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.199,
            0.402,
            0.884,
            0.445
          ],
          "content": "2. Draw two figures other than a circle and a square that have both reflection symmetry and rotational symmetry."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.2,
            0.447,
            0.669,
            0.468
          ],
          "content": "3. Draw, wherever possible, a rough sketch of:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.47,
            0.884,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": "a. A triangle with at least two lines of symmetry and at least two angles of symmetry."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.516,
            0.885,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": "b. A triangle with only one line of symmetry but not having rotational symmetry."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.561,
            0.833,
            0.604
          ],
          "content": "c. A quadrilateral with rotational symmetry but no reflection symmetry."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.606,
            0.833,
            0.65
          ],
          "content": "d. A quadrilateral with reflection symmetry but not having rotational symmetry."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.848,
            0.559,
            0.949,
            0.645
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_21_image_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.199,
            0.652,
            0.833,
            0.696
          ],
          "content": "4. In a figure, $6 0 ^ { \\circ }$ is the smallest angle of symmetry. What are the other angles of symmetry of this figure?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.2,
            0.698,
            0.885,
            0.741
          ],
          "content": "5. In a figure, $6 0 ^ { \\circ }$ is an angle of symmetry. The figure has two angles of symmetry less than 60°. What is its smallest angle of symmetry?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.2,
            0.743,
            0.884,
            0.787
          ],
          "content": "6. Can we have a figure with rotational symmetry whose smallest angle of symmetry is:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.79,
            0.307,
            0.808
          ],
          "content": "a. $4 5 ^ { \\circ } ?$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.812,
            0.308,
            0.831
          ],
          "content": "b. $1 7 ^ { \\circ } ?$"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.083,
